{"visualAudit":"01-candidates","data":{"grades":[{"subjectMatch":4,"learningValue":4,"composition":3,"thumbnailClarity":3,"contextualFit":4,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption should name both the fishpond in the foreground and the church in the distance, and give the 1993 date."],"reason":"Strongest choice. It shows two features the Examples text names, the former fishpond and the ruined church, together in the valley setting. That makes it more useful than the church-only views.","id":"6585802","total":18,"accepted":true},{"subjectMatch":3,"learningValue":3,"composition":4,"thumbnailClarity":4,"contextualFit":3,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption should note that the chancel is roofed but the church is otherwise ruined, so the image does not mislead.","Use only as a backup to the fishpond view."],"reason":"A clear, well-framed view of St Martin's church at Wharram Percy. Part of it still has a roof, so it shows the ruin less plainly than the interior view, and the fishpond does not appear.","id":"13199240","total":17,"accepted":true},{"subjectMatch":4,"learningValue":3,"composition":4,"thumbnailClarity":4,"contextualFit":3,"problems":[],"improvements":["Caption should say this is the roofless interior looking toward the tower."],"reason":"The roofless interior and tower show clearly that the church is a ruin. It shows only the church, with no fishpond or village setting, so it explains less than the fishpond view.","id":"183989393","total":18,"accepted":true}],"model":"anthropic/claude-opus-5-5","images":[{"id":"6585802","title":"Wharram Percy Geograph.jpg","description":"Picture of Wharram Percey, from this image at Geograph.org.uk.\nSubmitted to that site by Paul Allison\nTaken in 1993\n\nDescription: Deserted Medieval Village, Looking north from old Fish Pond","imageUrl":"https://upload.wikimedia.org/wikipedia/commons/6/6a/Wharram_Percy_Geograph.jpg?utm_source=commons.wikimedia.org&utm_campaign=imageinfo&utm_content=original","sourceUrl":"https://commons.